-- title:
--   Kernel degree of a special formal module endomorphism via v_{det}
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$. Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi \in \mathcal O$ irreducible, $\mathcal O$ complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, with $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi)) = r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$, and let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero field that is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $\mathrm{Onr}$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra carrying an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $\mathrm{Onr}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $\mathrm{Onr}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo that ideal, every monic polynomial over $\mathrm{Onr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo that ideal, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r}$ modulo that ideal. Let $v_{\det} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) be a group homomorphism with $v_{\det}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$. Let $\iota : W(\mathbb F_{r^2}) \to \mathrm{Onr}$ be a ring homomorphism and let $\Phi$ be a `FormalODModule` over $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$: a commutative formal group law $\Phi.F$ in two variables together with an action of $W(\mathbb F_{r^2})$ by endomorphisms and an endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi \circ \varpi = [r]$ and $\varpi \circ [a] = [\mathrm{Frobenius}(a)] \circ \varpi$. Assume $\Phi$ is special with respect to the composite of $\iota$ with reduction modulo $(r)$, meaning the submodules `lieZero` and `lieOne` attached to that homomorphism are complementary and each is an invertible $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$-module; and assume $\Phi$ has height $4$, i.e. the multiplication-by-$r$ series has kernel algebra finite and projective over $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ of rank $r^{4}$ after base change to any field. Let $E_0$ be a ring homomorphism from the centralizer of the endomorphisms $[a]$ together with $\varpi$ inside $\mathrm{End}(\Phi.F)$ to $M_2(K_0)$, assumed injective and commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ in the sense that for some $m$ every $A \in M_2(\mathcal O)$ has $r^{m}A$ in the image and $r^{m}E_0(e)$ lies in $M_2(\mathcal O)$ for every $e$. The conclusion: for every $e$ in that centralizer, every $M \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and every $k \in \mathbb Z$ with $E_0(e) = r^{k}M$, there is a natural number $h$ such that the power series underlying $e$ has kernel of degree $r^{h}$ (its kernel algebra is finite and projective over $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$, of dimension $r^{h}$ over any field it is base changed to) and $h = 4k + 2\,v_{\det}(M)$ as integers.
--
--   This is the height–determinant relation for endomorphisms of Drinfeld's special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module of height $4$: the degree of the kernel of an endomorphism is determined by the valuation of the determinant of its matrix under any $r^m$-commensurable embedding of the endomorphism ring into $M_2(K_0)$, here in the abstract $r$-adic frame rather than over $\mathbb Z_r$ itself. It is the input for the normalised-height form of the statement, which feeds the comparison of endomorphism heights with the $\mathrm{GL}_2$-action in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation.
